{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1173747-gamecraft-riddle-challenge-competitions-inspirations-found-in-anime","id":1173747,"title":"Gamecraft/Riddle/Challenge/Competitions Inspirations Found In Anime","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-01-06T06:57:37-08:00","id":1173747,"title":"Gamecraft/Riddle/Challenge/Competitions Inspirations Found In Anime","content":"One of the most distinctive and colorful aspect of Garou Culture is their resolution of conflicts and payment for requests through the tradition of non-violent games such as riddles, storytelling and song contests, puzzles, and even games of chess or poker. After all, even a game of football is ultimately a form of warfare substitute where you gain dominance (and even the respect) of your rivals without having to kill anyone in the process.<br /> <br /> And yet finding fresh variety and inspiration for non-violent conflict resolution, week in week out is also one of the most difficult tasks for even the most resourceful storytellers; which is probably why the muscle-headed Get of Fenris prerfer the good-old-fashioned way of just bashing the competition's head in and buying him a drink. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Fortunately, Japanese Animation is filled with examples that puts the resourcefulness, wit, skill and strength of character of its heroes to the test.<br /> This thread is intended as a place where examples can be pooled for storytellers to draw inspiration from.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Today's Example: &quot;Girls Und Panzer The Finale, Chapter One.&quot; (Released in Asian Theaters Just last Week)</b></u><br /> <br /> Our five heroines are a team of Tank Operators, analogous to a Garou Pack in their cooperation, camaraderie, trust, and varied skills/roles.<br /> They are on an archaeological search for an Ancient Tank in the lower decks of the city-sized aircraft carrier re-purposed as their hometown, where it's best described as a death-metal slum that crosses the scariest aspects of Mad Max and Blade Runner.<br /> Their Guide gets captured and imprisoned by the Five Pirate-Themed Delinquents who know of the location of the ancient tank.<br /> Who each sets a Competition that challenges the expertise of each heroine, with the prize of victory being the release of The Guide and Revealing The Location of the Tank they seek.<br /> <br /> <b>Challenge One: (Gamecraft) </b><br /> Flint holds out her left arm, from which hangs a bundle of ropes tied in an elaborate collage of knots and sneers &quot;Untie this if you can&quot;<br /> Fortunately, Akiyama Yukari the intelligence officer, an avid geek-encyclopedia of military knowledge (A Ragabash if you will) happily quips &quot;Ah! It's an anchor knot&quot; and unravels the collage of ropes in seconds as if she was unwrapping a candy from its wrapper.<br /> <br /> <b>Challenge Two: (Riddle)</b><br /> Rum performs an elaborate dance of signals with a red naval flag and a white naval flag at dizzying speed, and chuckles &quot;What did I just say?&quot;<br /> Fortunately, Takebe Saori, the radio operator of the heroine's tank and communications officer (Galliard) accurately and eloquently translates the Haiku-Poem Rum danced out, to the amazement of everyone present.<br /> <br /> <b>Challenge Three: (Contest of Strength)</b><br /> Cutlass the bartender engages Reizei Mako the Tank Driver (The calm and intelligent Theurge) in a ferocious rapid fire thumb-war, and was soundly beaten due to Mako having built up a superior acuity, dexterity and strength in her hands and fingers in her months of pushing and pulling tank levers, pullies and switches.<br /> <br /> <b>Challenge Four: (Combat: Albeit non-lethal)</b><br /> The burly Murakami loses her patience and charges Nishizumi Miho, the overall commander of the Heroines' Tank (The versatile and wise Philodox), and rains a barrage of ferocious punches upon her. Thankfully, due to her training in Martial Arts and the reflexes built dodging TANK CANNON ROUNDS from the top of turrets since CHILDHOOD, Miho efffortlessly dodges each and every blow and ACCIDENTALLY throw Murakami over her head after trying to bow in apology.<br /> <br /> <b>Challenge Fiver: Drinking Contest (A Gamecraft/Test of Endurance No doubt popular among Fianna and Get of Fenris or even Bone Gnawers)</b><br /> Silver, the &quot;Captain&quot; of the Pirate Posse, challenges Isuzu Hana, the Cannon Operator (The Brave and Determined Ahroun), to a contest where shot after shot of a <b>ferociously</b> spicy non-alcoholic (this being a Highschool Series and all) &quot;Pepper Rum&quot; is downed each round, with the first girl to yield being the loser. The FIRST shot-glass alone was enough to make each contestants' eye quiver with doubt.... dozens of shotglasses later, it seemed that Silver's experience with the spiciness of the concoction would win out the day... .but just as Hana is about to pass out, her calmnesss, focus and <i>strength of character</i> built from months of sniper-like cannon-operation allowed her to down her last shot-glass and graciously ask &quot;for another glass please&quot;.... and Silver's bravado alone was no longer enough to stop her from hitting the bar-room floor.<br /> <br /> And thus having Earned The Pirates' Respect by besting them in Contests of Skill, Wit, Strength, Courage and Strength of Character, not only do Our Heroines Free the Captured Guide, Gain a New Tank, but also said-Pirates' friendship and willingness to be the operators of said tank in the upcoming battle of said chapter.....<br /> <br /> ************************************************** ************************************<br /> <br /> Phew: REALLY wanted to share this scene with you fellas.<br /> Because its resemblance to the Garou Cultural Custom of Gamecraft/Riddle/Challenges is just UNCANNY. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Hopefully we can gather further examples of Contests challenging a Garou's Wit/Wisdom/Skill/Courage/Spirit in the thread that follows.<br /> <br /> Panzer Vor! (Tanks Forward!) <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4684,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","user":"Lin Liren","date":". 01-06-2018, 11:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","name":"Lin Liren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}